1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,387
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:54,346
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:55,306
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:00:57,183 --> 00:01:00,436
I just found it stuck between the seats.

6
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:05,733
So the last place she got off at
was Seocho Sejong Tower?

7
00:01:05,858 --> 00:01:09,653
That's right.
I think it was a little past 10:00.

8
00:01:09,779 --> 00:01:12,531
The lady was so drunk,
so I remember it clearly.

9
00:01:14,158 --> 00:01:14,992
Okay, thank you.

10
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:16,535
FRIENDLY RIDES
MEMORABLE EXITS

11
00:01:26,796 --> 00:01:30,049
25TH: CAN YOU SEND
AN EXTRA MILLION WON JUST THIS MONTH?

12
00:01:35,262 --> 00:01:37,723
Did you unlock it?
Who was the last caller?

13
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:39,517
I did.

14
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:43,813
NAMGUNG-TUSH

15
00:01:43,938 --> 00:01:45,022
TIN CAN BASTARD

16
00:01:46,857 --> 00:01:47,691
You're awake.

17
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:50,820
What?

18
00:01:51,654 --> 00:01:52,947
Why am I here?

19
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,574
Answer the phone first.

20
00:01:57,952 --> 00:01:59,954
I think it's your boyfriend.

21
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:05,042
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

22
00:02:06,001 --> 00:02:07,044
I guessed right.

23
00:02:09,839 --> 00:02:11,340
It is your boyfriend.

24
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:20,558
What now?

25
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,434
If you want, I can decline--

26
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:26,939
Hey, Namgung.

27
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:28,482
Where are you?

28
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:30,734
I'll go home. We'll talk there.

29
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:32,903
-Where are you? I'll pick you up.
-Is it her?

30
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:34,947
-Where is she? Who is she with?
-Hold on.

31
00:02:35,072 --> 00:02:37,992
I'll explain at home.
I'll be there in 30 minutes.

32
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:40,578
Hello? Mi-do--

33
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:47,334
She's coming home.

34
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:57,011
Explain what happened.

35
00:02:58,762 --> 00:02:59,930
You don't remember?

36
00:03:00,848 --> 00:03:02,391
Wow.

37
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,435
I guess you really don't remember.

38
00:03:10,232 --> 00:03:11,525
Still nothing?

39
00:03:15,571 --> 00:03:18,157
Are you going to meet with Mr. Seo
and self-destruct?

40
00:03:19,450 --> 00:03:20,993
Ugh, seriously.

41
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:23,370
What are you going to do there?

42
00:03:32,504 --> 00:03:33,547
Director Lee.

43
00:03:35,591 --> 00:03:36,425
Wait.

44
00:03:45,309 --> 00:03:47,645
VACANT

45
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:56,862
Damn it.

46
00:04:30,813 --> 00:04:32,523
ELEVATOR UNDER MAINTENANCE

47
00:04:32,648 --> 00:04:33,691
Please check.

48
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:36,151
Repairs are complete.

49
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:37,319
Understood.

50
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:53,836
I'm very lucky.

51
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:56,171
What are the odds

52
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:59,425
of the elevator breaking down
right at that moment?

53
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,302
For the record, I didn't do it.

54
00:05:02,428 --> 00:05:05,556
Even I couldn't have predicted
a variable like that.

55
00:05:23,449 --> 00:05:24,658
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO
SEND FILE

56
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,827
What are you doing?

57
00:05:26,952 --> 00:05:29,121
Securing evidence
for a false accusation claim.

58
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:33,709
I'll send the settlement agreement
by courier today.

59
00:05:35,753 --> 00:05:37,963
Congratulations. You won.

60
00:05:44,511 --> 00:05:47,181
There are no hallway cameras
on this floor.

61
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,478
Take the stairs, not the elevator.

62
00:05:53,479 --> 00:05:56,148
And avoid the lobby.
Go to the third basement level.

63
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:58,442
There's an elevator to the next building.

64
00:05:58,567 --> 00:05:59,693
Why?

65
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:03,280
Because Seo Ju-hyeok
can't find out that I was here?

66
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:05,699
Fine.

67
00:06:05,824 --> 00:06:08,368
I'll take the stairs
to the third basement level.

68
00:06:13,207 --> 00:06:14,625
When you send the settlement,

69
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:15,918
have an expert provide proof

70
00:06:16,043 --> 00:06:18,796
that the files were deleted
from your cloud and hard drives.

71
00:06:18,921 --> 00:06:21,131
I will. Get out of my way.

72
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:23,842
Hey!

73
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,427
What?

74
00:06:25,552 --> 00:06:28,222
What else is there? Just say it!

75
00:06:31,183 --> 00:06:32,309
Once you leave,

76
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:37,523
will we never see each other again?

77
00:07:10,848 --> 00:07:16,728
5. ARE THERE ANY
UNTOLD STORIES BETWEEN US?

78
00:07:16,854 --> 00:07:19,439
Look, this is the office,

79
00:07:19,565 --> 00:07:21,441
and this is the sofa I slept on.

80
00:07:23,277 --> 00:07:25,529
And he just sat there and did work.

81
00:07:26,572 --> 00:07:29,116
I swear. Absolutely nothing happened.

82
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:33,829
I'm sorry I worried you.

83
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:37,166
I was so stressed
about the settlement agreement.

84
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:39,376
I was drunk and wasn't thinking.

85
00:07:43,922 --> 00:07:45,799
I think he tried to trick me

86
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:48,552
into signing the settlement
while I was drunk.

87
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:50,262
What?

88
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:52,181
You know that lawyer?

89
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:54,516
That bastard is like a tin can.

90
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,727
Trash that'll take
at least 200 years to rot.

91
00:07:56,852 --> 00:07:58,353
What do you mean? Be clear.

92
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:01,148
But technically, I did start it.

93
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:04,443
I found out his weakness by accident

94
00:08:04,568 --> 00:08:07,487
and blackmailed him
to change the contract in my favor.

95
00:08:12,409 --> 00:08:13,577
Of course,

96
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,288
I really regret it now.

97
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:19,374
I'm really reflecting on what I did.

98
00:08:21,919 --> 00:08:22,878
Hey!

99
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:27,966
Give me his number.

100
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:30,093
Hey.

101
00:08:30,219 --> 00:08:31,595
Should I ask Oh Yeon-ju?

102
00:08:32,554 --> 00:08:34,556
I'm telling you, nothing happened.

103
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:36,475
After sending the settlement today,

104
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,101
I'll never have to see him again.

105
00:08:38,227 --> 00:08:40,187
So you expect me to let it go?

106
00:08:40,312 --> 00:08:41,647
Then what should I do?

107
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:45,234
Walk into the law firm
holding your hand like a preschooler?

108
00:08:45,359 --> 00:08:47,444
That's what you say after making me worry?

109
00:08:47,569 --> 00:08:49,655
I'm acting like this because I'm sorry.

110
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:51,365
The guilt is killing me.

111
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:52,866
You don't even look sorry.

112
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:54,701
Then what should I do? Huh?

113
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:55,994
Should I just cry?

114
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,038
Yes, cry! Go on!

115
00:08:58,997 --> 00:09:00,624
Ugh, seriously.

116
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:02,459
Damn it.

117
00:09:21,853 --> 00:09:24,106
I'm sorry for worrying you, sweetie.

118
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:27,067
But as you saw in the video earlier,

119
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:29,403
nothing really happened, sweetie.

120
00:09:29,528 --> 00:09:31,822
I know. That's not the point, sweetie.

121
00:09:31,947 --> 00:09:33,615
Don't force yourself to settle, sweetie.

122
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:36,702
No, I also just wanted
to end it here, sweetie.

123
00:09:36,827 --> 00:09:39,037
I guess it's for the best, sweetie.

124
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:40,205
Just like that, sweetie?

125
00:09:40,747 --> 00:09:42,916
Why? We'll go to trial
if you want, sweetie.

126
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:44,418
Oh no, sweetie.

127
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:46,795
I could be writing instead, sweetie.

128
00:09:47,796 --> 00:09:51,049
Alcohol is what caused
all of this, sweetie.

129
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:52,259
I'm taking

130
00:09:53,051 --> 00:09:55,095
a three-month break
from drinking, sweetie.

131
00:09:55,887 --> 00:09:57,264
Only three months, sweetie?

132
00:09:57,389 --> 00:09:59,725
It's not just any three months, sweetie.

133
00:09:59,850 --> 00:10:01,768
It includes Christmas,
the end of the year,

134
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,103
and the New Year, sweetie.

135
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:05,939
I'm saying I'll give all that up, sweetie.

136
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:08,108
Oh, that's huge for sure, sweetie.

137
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,361
I said I'm sorry, sweetie.

138
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:22,914
-Stop, I get it.
-I'm trying here.

139
00:10:35,761 --> 00:10:36,636
Namgung.

140
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:39,264
Did you wait long yesterday?

141
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:43,769
No.

142
00:10:44,728 --> 00:10:45,562
Sorry.

143
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:50,359
Let's meet on the second snowfall
this year instead of the first.

144
00:10:50,484 --> 00:10:51,860
I'll be waiting for you.

145
00:10:57,366 --> 00:10:58,408
Mi-do.

146
00:11:01,328 --> 00:11:02,704
I was wondering.

147
00:11:06,041 --> 00:11:06,917
Have you…

148
00:11:07,334 --> 00:11:10,837
25TH: CAN YOU SEND
AN EXTRA MILLION WON JUST THIS MONTH?

149
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:20,013
Never mind. Let's talk after work.

150
00:11:28,522 --> 00:11:30,107
Bambi!

151
00:11:30,816 --> 00:11:31,650
Bambi.

152
00:11:31,775 --> 00:11:34,152
Where did she go?

153
00:11:34,277 --> 00:11:35,112
Bambi!

154
00:11:36,696 --> 00:11:37,823
Hey, move.

155
00:11:41,368 --> 00:11:42,202
Okay.

156
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:43,995
LOVE EAT

157
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:47,916
Come on.

158
00:12:05,267 --> 00:12:07,227
City Hall raided us recently,

159
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:09,729
so she's gotten more cautious.

160
00:12:10,814 --> 00:12:13,066
Oh, no wonder.

161
00:12:14,609 --> 00:12:16,820
By the way, how do you know Bambi?

162
00:12:16,945 --> 00:12:19,197
It's not Bambi. It's Pudgy.

163
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:23,034
Plenty of people feed her besides us.

164
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,412
Look how chubby she is.

165
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:30,750
Did you know I was feeding Bambi?

166
00:12:31,543 --> 00:12:34,588
I said it's not Bambi. It's Pudgy.

167
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:36,173
Pudgy?

168
00:12:36,298 --> 00:12:37,883
Such tragic naming skills.

169
00:12:40,886 --> 00:12:42,929
The mom wasn't caught, right?

170
00:12:43,847 --> 00:12:44,848
Oh, she ran away.

171
00:12:46,558 --> 00:12:47,434
I saw her.

172
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:49,352
She hasn't returned.

173
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:51,229
She's not very motherly.

174
00:12:54,483 --> 00:12:55,692
By the way,

175
00:12:55,817 --> 00:12:58,862
why did you go to
the Cheonan factory this morning?

176
00:12:59,529 --> 00:13:00,780
That wasn't in the schedule.

177
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:04,034
I went to explain the new seasoning mix.

178
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:08,288
It's not what you think,
so don't get ahead of yourself.

179
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:13,627
Why don't you take another shot
at becoming a reporter?

180
00:13:13,752 --> 00:13:15,045
That was your dream.

181
00:13:16,713 --> 00:13:18,298
You clearly got rejected,

182
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:20,926
and now you're trying
to fulfill your potential here.

183
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:23,386
Give it another try. You're still young.

184
00:13:24,304 --> 00:13:25,972
I never even applied.

185
00:13:26,097 --> 00:13:28,391
So I never got rejected.

186
00:13:29,059 --> 00:13:31,269
I specifically aimed
for Hunmin Confectionery,

187
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:35,524
and I was capable enough
to get hired that same year.

188
00:13:36,483 --> 00:13:38,693
Wasn't your dream to be a reporter?

189
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:42,364
Well, briefly in high school.

190
00:13:42,989 --> 00:13:44,115
Just for a while.

191
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,619
Come on.
You wanted to be Korea's Amanpour

192
00:13:47,744 --> 00:13:50,539
and recited "A Night Counting Stars"
all day in the pavilion.

193
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:52,541
I memorized that whole poem
because of you.

194
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,835
When did I ever do that?
I did no such thing.

195
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:57,504
Let's go in.

196
00:14:01,633 --> 00:14:03,510
How are you holding up? How's the injury?

197
00:14:04,553 --> 00:14:06,596
Oh, I'm fine.

198
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:08,557
Jeez.

199
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:10,767
Get it checked out.

200
00:14:12,561 --> 00:14:13,395
Okay.

201
00:14:16,398 --> 00:14:18,858
Back off.
We're near work. People will talk.

202
00:14:18,984 --> 00:14:20,485
-Hurry.
-Oh, right.

203
00:14:21,361 --> 00:14:22,237
Three steps.

204
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:23,446
Three steps?

205
00:14:24,364 --> 00:14:26,241
-More, more.
-More?

206
00:14:26,950 --> 00:14:28,034
That's good.

207
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:41,923
Gosh, seriously.
I play along, and you cross the line.

208
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:49,180
Damn it, seriously.

209
00:14:53,393 --> 00:14:55,562
KO MUN-YEONG LAB

210
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:05,697
I only have eight minutes.

211
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,282
So don't argue. Just listen.

212
00:15:07,407 --> 00:15:09,451
Are you kidding me?

213
00:15:09,576 --> 00:15:10,827
Then text me. I'm busy too.

214
00:15:10,952 --> 00:15:13,788
I'll cut this month's principal
and interest by 10%.

215
00:15:14,414 --> 00:15:15,957
Go on. Tell me.

216
00:15:28,553 --> 00:15:29,596
Thank you.

217
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,478
So…

218
00:15:37,062 --> 00:15:39,481
Use contraception properly!

219
00:15:39,606 --> 00:15:40,523
KO MUN-YEONG CHALLENGE

220
00:15:40,649 --> 00:15:42,317
-Use your socials…
-Properly!

221
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,110
-Properly!
-Properly!

222
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:45,612
Properly-ly-ly!

223
00:15:45,737 --> 00:15:46,780
Don't do anything…

224
00:15:46,905 --> 00:15:47,947
…you'll regret!

225
00:15:48,073 --> 00:15:50,575
…you'll regret-ret-ret!

226
00:15:52,661 --> 00:15:54,412
How are you handling the kid?

227
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:57,707
It would've hit the news
if PR hadn't found it so fast.

228
00:15:57,832 --> 00:16:00,502
Then why did you do
something you would regret?

229
00:16:01,086 --> 00:16:03,463
It's trending again.
The Ko Mun-yeong drunk challenge.

230
00:16:03,588 --> 00:16:06,841
When Sang-su
got counseling for this last time,

231
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:10,178
I thought he and I worked it out,
but I guess not.

232
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:12,764
He should go back to counseling.

233
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:17,602
Come on, he was just having fun.
You're overreacting again.

234
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:19,145
Overreacting?

235
00:16:20,397 --> 00:16:21,439
Yes, overreacting.

236
00:16:22,273 --> 00:16:23,692
Don't you know Sang-su?

237
00:16:24,359 --> 00:16:25,985
He doesn't think much of it.

238
00:16:26,111 --> 00:16:28,655
It's just a fun trend.

239
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,990
His friends do it, so he just joined in.

240
00:16:31,116 --> 00:16:35,120
3:00 p.m. on the 3rd,
7:00 on the 9th, or 11:00 on the 11th.

241
00:16:35,245 --> 00:16:36,329
Pick a time.

242
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:38,748
I'm scheduling a parent-child session.

243
00:16:38,873 --> 00:16:40,458
Come on, that's overkill.

244
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:42,961
Stop reading so much into nothing.

245
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:49,175
You haven't changed.

246
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:52,554
You got divorced over "nothing,"

247
00:16:52,679 --> 00:16:56,599
and you still treat everything
like it's no big deal.

248
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,687
Ever been slapped with a burger?

249
00:17:02,188 --> 00:17:04,524
In a place full of middle schoolers?

250
00:17:05,567 --> 00:17:07,318
Ever been slapped like that?

251
00:17:09,070 --> 00:17:10,113
I want a burger.

252
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:12,866
I haven't been able
to eat a burger since then.

253
00:17:12,991 --> 00:17:13,992
I'm traumatized.

254
00:17:14,117 --> 00:17:15,952
Is this about Sang-su
doing that challenge?

255
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:17,871
Should I talk to him?

256
00:17:17,996 --> 00:17:20,248
We were coming back from a nice trip

257
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:22,792
and didn't want to cook at home.

258
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:27,213
We decided to grab burgers on the way,
so we went in.

259
00:17:27,338 --> 00:17:29,424
But just because
I didn't grab enough ketchup…

260
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:33,094
she threw a burger at me
and asked for a divorce.

261
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:35,346
You said things were rocky on the trip.

262
00:17:35,472 --> 00:17:37,223
It's not that I'm not over her.

263
00:17:37,348 --> 00:17:38,767
I'm just genuinely curious.

264
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:42,395
She didn't leave me
even when I failed the civil service exam.

265
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,688
Right.

266
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:48,568
When you blew the store deposit
trading overseas stocks,

267
00:17:48,693 --> 00:17:50,737
she let it slide without a word.

268
00:17:50,862 --> 00:17:53,406
No, there was definitely another reason.

269
00:17:54,282 --> 00:17:55,366
I'm sure of it.

270
00:17:56,826 --> 00:17:58,036
Do you really not know?

271
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:05,335
How would I know if you don't?

272
00:18:07,796 --> 00:18:09,088
Try calling my baby.

273
00:18:09,214 --> 00:18:11,883
His stomachaches seem to linger
this time of year.

274
00:18:12,634 --> 00:18:13,927
Your baby's 30 this year.

275
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:15,094
You call him.

276
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:19,808
-What are you doing?
-Being clingy.

277
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:24,687
Hold on.

278
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,023
Stop sending gift cards.

279
00:18:27,148 --> 00:18:27,982
Adult movies…

280
00:18:29,317 --> 00:18:30,819
I don't know anything about them.

281
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:33,696
24 Hours Is Never Enough,
365 Days Isn't Enough,

282
00:18:33,822 --> 00:18:34,656
Secrets of Hiking,

283
00:18:34,781 --> 00:18:36,157
In-Laws Are Fine.

284
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:38,201
Do you know any others besides these?

285
00:18:38,326 --> 00:18:39,744
I don't.

286
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:43,206
Without knowing her pay, how would I know
how many film contracts she signed?

287
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:45,625
Hey!

288
00:18:46,209 --> 00:18:47,502
You didn't, did you?

289
00:18:47,627 --> 00:18:49,045
Dude, if Mi-do finds out

290
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:51,714
that I told you about the studio,
I'm dead.

291
00:18:52,382 --> 00:18:54,050
Hey! Namgung!

292
00:18:54,175 --> 00:18:55,009
Nam--

293
00:19:01,391 --> 00:19:03,852
Director Lee,
did you see the posting from Danwol City?

294
00:19:04,519 --> 00:19:06,813
You know your script,  My Dear Dictator?

295
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:08,982
You should submit it.

296
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:10,859
Danwol City's orchestra is quite famous,

297
00:19:10,984 --> 00:19:12,986
so it's a perfect fit for your work.

298
00:19:13,111 --> 00:19:14,654
Oh, that's a great idea.

299
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:17,574
You should submit it.
Have you revised it at all?

300
00:19:20,577 --> 00:19:22,287
You guys must not be busy.

301
00:19:22,412 --> 00:19:24,497
Is pre-production too easy for you?

302
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:27,458
Or did Director Gong
get more flexible with age?

303
00:19:27,584 --> 00:19:29,794
Filming starts late next year,

304
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:31,337
so we have some time.

305
00:19:32,046 --> 00:19:34,173
Anyway, I looked at the posting,

306
00:19:34,299 --> 00:19:36,050
and the requirements are practically…

307
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:39,971
ATTACK ON THE WALKING TRIPOD

308
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:54,235
Yes, Namgung.

309
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:57,655
She must have signed
with another studio. What do we do?

310
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:02,785
You worked so hard with that studio
to get her contract canceled.

311
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,496
I pitched Danwol City.

312
00:20:05,622 --> 00:20:08,124
I keep telling her to do indie films,

313
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:09,250
but it's not easy.

314
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:11,920
Once I find out the new studio,

315
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:14,047
I'll let you know right away…

316
00:20:20,511 --> 00:20:22,972
Namgung, what do I do?

317
00:20:23,097 --> 00:20:25,141
Director Lee is right here.

318
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:27,685
Okay, you've got my back--

319
00:20:27,810 --> 00:20:30,229
Hello? Namgung? Namgung!

320
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:33,900
Since when did Namgung Ho
become your boss?

321
00:20:36,069 --> 00:20:39,781
When we met at the police station,

322
00:20:39,906 --> 00:20:43,409
he gave me money for a taxi,

323
00:20:43,534 --> 00:20:46,120
and I gave him my number.

324
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:48,373
That's how we connected…

325
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:04,514
Did you pay the studio
to cancel my contract?

326
00:21:05,974 --> 00:21:07,225
Yeah.

327
00:21:07,350 --> 00:21:10,353
I paid 10% more
than your advance to cancel it.

328
00:21:11,854 --> 00:21:13,356
But it was all for nothing,

329
00:21:13,481 --> 00:21:16,359
because you went and signed
another contract.

330
00:21:16,484 --> 00:21:18,695
I know you hate me shooting adult films.

331
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:22,532
Sorry I didn't tell you
about the remaining contract.

332
00:21:22,657 --> 00:21:23,825
But Namgung,

333
00:21:25,076 --> 00:21:26,369
this isn't right.

334
00:21:27,161 --> 00:21:28,705
You crossed the line.

335
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:30,540
For how long?

336
00:21:32,458 --> 00:21:34,794
-What?
-How long…

337
00:21:37,463 --> 00:21:38,715
have you been paying her?

338
00:21:40,133 --> 00:21:42,260
It's been two years, as far as I know.

339
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:45,430
Because that's when you started
directing adult films.

340
00:21:48,141 --> 00:21:50,101
Why didn't you tell me?

341
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,895
Why didn't you tell me and just…

342
00:21:58,067 --> 00:21:59,819
I'm not mad at you.

343
00:22:01,404 --> 00:22:03,281
She must have used me to threaten you.

344
00:22:03,406 --> 00:22:06,117
Saying she'd come find me
if you didn't pay her.

345
00:22:06,868 --> 00:22:07,994
It's so obvious

346
00:22:08,828 --> 00:22:10,747
what that woman must have done to you.

347
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:13,750
I did pay her living expenses.

348
00:22:14,876 --> 00:22:17,879
But it has nothing to do with Hwa-young.

349
00:22:18,004 --> 00:22:19,756
Send me the total by next week.

350
00:22:20,590 --> 00:22:21,632
I'll pay you back.

351
00:22:21,758 --> 00:22:22,633
Hey.

352
00:22:24,010 --> 00:22:25,511
Why would you pay me?

353
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:27,597
I didn't do it expecting you to pay me.

354
00:22:27,722 --> 00:22:28,598
Take it.

355
00:22:31,142 --> 00:22:32,935
Or I won't be able to look at you.

356
00:22:41,194 --> 00:22:44,072
Why would you ruin your career
because of me?

357
00:22:45,448 --> 00:22:49,827
I know better than anyone
how much films mean to you.

358
00:22:53,539 --> 00:22:55,374
Why should you have to do that?

359
00:23:00,797 --> 00:23:01,881
Namgung.

360
00:23:07,345 --> 00:23:08,471
Don't be ridiculous.

361
00:23:09,138 --> 00:23:13,518
My pride as a director hasn't been ruined
just because I directed a few adult films.

362
00:23:14,769 --> 00:23:15,603
Hey.

363
00:23:16,312 --> 00:23:17,772
I'm Lee Mi-do.

364
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:21,400
I don't let things like that sway me.

365
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:22,902
Okay?

366
00:23:25,196 --> 00:23:27,281
I'm too ashamed to look at you.

367
00:23:32,662 --> 00:23:35,414
I could go crazy
from how sorry and embarrassed I am.

368
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:37,375
What's so embarrassing about this?

369
00:23:38,376 --> 00:23:40,294
What's really embarrassing is

370
00:23:41,003 --> 00:23:44,674
ten-year-old you going to camp
and peeing his pants after seeing a bat.

371
00:23:44,799 --> 00:23:45,633
Hey!

372
00:23:46,175 --> 00:23:47,009
Jeez.

373
00:23:49,804 --> 00:23:50,721
Namgung.

374
00:23:51,764 --> 00:23:53,432
Even if I went back in time,

375
00:23:55,268 --> 00:23:56,978
I'd still make the same choice.

376
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:00,815
I don't regret it.

377
00:24:04,026 --> 00:24:05,153
I'm sorry.

378
00:24:06,654 --> 00:24:08,406
I didn't even know.

379
00:24:10,366 --> 00:24:11,784
I said awful things to you,

380
00:24:12,702 --> 00:24:13,870
hurt you,

381
00:24:14,829 --> 00:24:15,872
and lashed out.

382
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:19,917
I'm sorry.

383
00:24:22,253 --> 00:24:24,380
You are?

384
00:24:28,259 --> 00:24:29,927
If you're that sorry…

385
00:24:31,095 --> 00:24:32,763
you're doing the recycling for a month.

386
00:24:33,848 --> 00:24:35,308
I already do that.

387
00:24:35,433 --> 00:24:37,685
Hmm, then dishes for a month.

388
00:24:38,394 --> 00:24:39,812
I already do that too.

389
00:24:39,937 --> 00:24:42,064
Then let's call it even.

390
00:24:46,819 --> 00:24:47,987
Listen.

391
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:51,824
Don't you dare use this as an excuse
to go see Hwa-young.

392
00:24:51,949 --> 00:24:52,783
Got it?

393
00:24:57,872 --> 00:24:58,706
You didn't, right?

394
00:24:58,831 --> 00:25:00,666
I hired a lawyer.

395
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:05,129
I'm going to do everything I legally can.

396
00:25:06,505 --> 00:25:07,798
I'm ending this for good.

397
00:25:09,217 --> 00:25:12,845
So I think I need to see her
one last time.

398
00:25:15,431 --> 00:25:17,308
Just let me do this once.

399
00:25:22,813 --> 00:25:23,898
I'll go with you.

400
00:25:26,859 --> 00:25:29,654
I don't want you to see me
with that woman.

401
00:25:35,326 --> 00:25:36,244
Mi-do.

402
00:25:38,329 --> 00:25:40,498
I'll really end it this time.

403
00:25:43,834 --> 00:25:44,961
Just wait for me.

404
00:25:50,967 --> 00:25:51,801
Okay.

405
00:25:59,850 --> 00:26:01,018
Oh, wait a second.

406
00:26:04,021 --> 00:26:04,897
Here.

407
00:26:07,358 --> 00:26:08,234
What's this?

408
00:26:09,068 --> 00:26:10,278
A voice recorder.

409
00:26:10,403 --> 00:26:13,906
Turn it on when you see her, just in case.

410
00:26:14,031 --> 00:26:16,200
For the record, this isn't illegal.

411
00:26:18,327 --> 00:26:19,203
Namgung.

412
00:26:20,621 --> 00:26:22,456
Only say half.

413
00:26:26,669 --> 00:26:30,423
Only say half
of what you want to say to Hwa-young.

414
00:26:33,217 --> 00:26:35,928
Pouring everything out
might feel good in the moment,

415
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,180
but you'll hurt more later.

416
00:26:42,059 --> 00:26:43,644
My Mi-do has grown up.

417
00:26:44,270 --> 00:26:46,063
Someone raised me well.

418
00:26:56,282 --> 00:26:59,285
I won't leave you to suffer alone anymore.

419
00:27:02,413 --> 00:27:03,956
I'll protect you.

420
00:27:20,806 --> 00:27:22,641
When revising a script,

421
00:27:22,767 --> 00:27:26,354
some scenes inevitably get deleted
for the sake of pacing and length.

422
00:27:26,479 --> 00:27:28,230
MY DEAR DICTATOR VER. 12

423
00:27:28,898 --> 00:27:30,566
The so-called deleted scenes.

424
00:27:31,609 --> 00:27:35,196
Even without these scenes,
the story still flows and connects well.

425
00:27:35,905 --> 00:27:38,407
They are unknown only to the audience.

426
00:27:38,532 --> 00:27:41,994
Our lives are also made up
by deleted scenes such as these.

427
00:27:42,119 --> 00:27:44,246
The ones we want to hide from others.

428
00:27:44,372 --> 00:27:45,456
DELETED SCENES

429
00:27:45,581 --> 00:27:47,625
The untold stories only I know about.

430
00:28:04,183 --> 00:28:05,184
Hey, Namgung.

431
00:28:05,309 --> 00:28:08,104
It's cold. You bundled up, right?

432
00:28:08,229 --> 00:28:10,856
He's sick in bed. Why would he dress up?

433
00:28:10,981 --> 00:28:13,401
Hey, how sick are you to skip fishing?

434
00:28:13,526 --> 00:28:14,652
Are you faking it?

435
00:28:14,777 --> 00:28:16,362
No, I'm not.

436
00:28:16,487 --> 00:28:17,655
Hey.

437
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:20,282
Did Yeong-do fight with his ex-wife?

438
00:28:20,408 --> 00:28:22,701
Wow, my baby is so perceptive.

439
00:28:22,827 --> 00:28:24,870
I'll bring you some good food later.

440
00:28:24,995 --> 00:28:26,997
Don't cry about your stomachache.

441
00:28:27,123 --> 00:28:28,916
-Okay.
-There you go. Good boy.

442
00:28:29,041 --> 00:28:29,917
See you.

443
00:28:57,153 --> 00:28:58,946
Who leaves early for counseling?

444
00:28:59,864 --> 00:29:01,490
Mom put you up to this again?

445
00:29:02,908 --> 00:29:04,910
Rehearse what we practiced earlier.

446
00:29:07,580 --> 00:29:10,916
"All my friends were doing it,
so I did it for fun."

447
00:29:11,542 --> 00:29:12,960
"I didn't think much of it."

448
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:16,881
Say exactly that
in front of Mom and the counselor.

449
00:29:17,006 --> 00:29:20,050
-You promised.
-You keep your promise, Dad.

450
00:29:20,176 --> 00:29:22,803
I'm really going to
stay up all night and play games.

451
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:24,638
Don't you dare nag me.

452
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:26,098
Only for a month, though.

453
00:29:27,516 --> 00:29:30,769
Mom wouldn't get hurt
even if she found out anyway.

454
00:29:31,687 --> 00:29:33,564
Do you really not know Mom?

455
00:29:36,734 --> 00:29:38,444
Your mom will die of shock.

456
00:29:45,910 --> 00:29:49,205
If she finds out you filmed that
to hurt her feelings,

457
00:29:50,789 --> 00:29:52,541
she'll literally die.

458
00:29:54,335 --> 00:29:55,794
Hey, Driver.

459
00:29:56,545 --> 00:29:58,380
You must have seen it too.

460
00:29:58,506 --> 00:30:00,633
365 Days Isn't Enough.

461
00:30:00,758 --> 00:30:04,845
That was the number-one hit film
on IPTV last year…

462
00:30:08,766 --> 00:30:10,059
It's you again?

463
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:14,021
How many days has it been now?

464
00:30:14,146 --> 00:30:16,649
At the car wash,
and as a designated driver…

465
00:30:16,774 --> 00:30:18,734
How long will you keep bothering me?

466
00:30:18,859 --> 00:30:21,570
Until you cancel
Director Lee Mi-do's remaining contract.

467
00:30:23,864 --> 00:30:25,866
You're so damn persistent.

468
00:30:26,659 --> 00:30:29,286
What's your relationship
with Director Lee Mi-do anyway?

469
00:30:30,287 --> 00:30:32,331
-Are you her boyfriend?
-I'm a fan.

470
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:33,457
Huh?

471
00:30:35,167 --> 00:30:36,335
I'm her number one fan.

472
00:30:42,466 --> 00:30:46,804
Damn, that's beautiful. So damn beautiful.

473
00:31:04,405 --> 00:31:06,156
Don't ever contact me again.

474
00:31:07,950 --> 00:31:09,618
That's what I came here to say.

475
00:31:18,419 --> 00:31:20,546
Medical report, photos of bruises.

476
00:31:20,671 --> 00:31:21,505
Hwa-young.

477
00:31:22,172 --> 00:31:24,925
Don't use things like that
to get Namgung's sympathy.

478
00:31:26,468 --> 00:31:28,512
If you contact us one more time,

479
00:31:29,930 --> 00:31:31,473
I won't just sit back.

480
00:31:50,451 --> 00:31:51,577
Mom!

481
00:31:57,249 --> 00:31:58,375
Namgung.

482
00:31:59,043 --> 00:32:01,670
That day, I met
the seven-year-old you again.

483
00:32:02,796 --> 00:32:06,050
The seven-year-old you
that I couldn't protect.

484
00:32:20,189 --> 00:32:21,023
COURT

485
00:32:21,148 --> 00:32:22,274
I will read the verdict.

486
00:32:22,399 --> 00:32:25,361
As there is no proof that the defendant,
Line Intercontinental,

487
00:32:25,486 --> 00:32:28,113
intentionally disregarded

488
00:32:28,238 --> 00:32:30,908
the damage to the component,

489
00:32:31,033 --> 00:32:33,202
and as it is difficult to conclude

490
00:32:33,327 --> 00:32:36,121
that the component
caused the vehicle defect,

491
00:32:36,246 --> 00:32:38,832
causality cannot be established.

492
00:32:38,957 --> 00:32:42,753
Therefore, all of the plaintiff's claims
are dismissed.

493
00:32:47,549 --> 00:32:50,511
Chairman Ko of Jisang did this, didn't he?

494
00:32:50,636 --> 00:32:53,597
His temper is really something.

495
00:32:53,722 --> 00:32:56,558
Fifty billion won's worth of land
is about to vanish.

496
00:32:57,810 --> 00:33:00,104
A busted forehead means he's being nice.

497
00:33:02,398 --> 00:33:03,607
Was it Kim Jeong-hwan?

498
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:06,110
The whistleblower from Line.

499
00:33:07,820 --> 00:33:09,321
We're looking for him.

500
00:33:10,030 --> 00:33:12,616
There's no departure record,
so he should still be in the country.

501
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:16,829
We won the trial,

502
00:33:16,954 --> 00:33:20,082
but if this guy happens to show up,

503
00:33:20,207 --> 00:33:21,667
we're in trouble.

504
00:33:23,043 --> 00:33:26,255
All of Jisang's internal
verification reports have been destroyed,

505
00:33:26,380 --> 00:33:28,090
and the three researchers who testified

506
00:33:28,966 --> 00:33:30,843
were all sent overseas.

507
00:33:31,802 --> 00:33:34,221
The audit logs, transaction history,

508
00:33:34,346 --> 00:33:37,516
and raw packet records
were deleted and reformatted,

509
00:33:38,892 --> 00:33:40,060
so there's no need to worry.

510
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:42,688
Just to be safe,
find him as soon as possible.

511
00:33:42,813 --> 00:33:44,189
Understood.

512
00:33:52,406 --> 00:33:54,241
She's so hard to read.

513
00:33:55,325 --> 00:33:57,619
She begged to be back
in the director's chair,

514
00:33:58,704 --> 00:33:59,830
and now she refuses?

515
00:33:59,955 --> 00:34:02,374
I know. Now she's refusing.

516
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,460
Why are you so calm?

517
00:34:06,545 --> 00:34:08,422
If the truth about my dad gets out,

518
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:10,340
don't you know it would affect Ju-hyeok?

519
00:34:11,216 --> 00:34:12,718
Then we'll kill her.

520
00:34:13,343 --> 00:34:15,471
Isn't that the best way to shut her up?

521
00:34:15,596 --> 00:34:17,055
Are you crazy?

522
00:34:18,724 --> 00:34:20,434
Are you out of your mind?

523
00:34:22,853 --> 00:34:23,771
Exactly.

524
00:34:25,272 --> 00:34:26,774
That's how you're supposed to react.

525
00:34:36,867 --> 00:34:37,951
Director Lee Mi-do.

526
00:34:39,161 --> 00:34:40,871
Director Lee Mi-do just walked by.

527
00:34:41,872 --> 00:34:43,123
Did you see her?

528
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:54,802
A master in Hadong
cultivated this  ujeon  tea.

529
00:34:55,803 --> 00:34:59,681
You mean the foreigner we saw
at the tea plantation last time?

530
00:34:59,807 --> 00:35:00,891
That's right.

531
00:35:01,016 --> 00:35:04,394
He's one of the few
certified tea masters in the UK.

532
00:35:05,020 --> 00:35:08,565
He's a very important person
who gets invited to British royal events.

533
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:10,400
For the past two years,

534
00:35:10,526 --> 00:35:12,986
he's been handling the tea leaves

535
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:15,405
from cupping to fermentation.

536
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:18,909
-No wonder.
-So the entire hectare of land we saw

537
00:35:19,034 --> 00:35:20,452
belongs to you?

538
00:35:21,745 --> 00:35:24,206
It's been in my family
since my grandfather.

539
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:28,836
This is my first business venture,
so I'm quite worried.

540
00:35:28,961 --> 00:35:31,171
Wow, that's so cool!

541
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:32,923
No wonder you look so elegant.

542
00:35:33,048 --> 00:35:35,509
You have a certain presence.
Don't we all agree?

543
00:35:38,679 --> 00:35:40,264
Can I get a taste too?

544
00:35:43,767 --> 00:35:47,187
Oh my, what brings
a young man like you to this place?

545
00:35:47,312 --> 00:35:48,355
He's handsome.

546
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:50,232
I'm very interested in tea.

547
00:36:14,006 --> 00:36:15,757
The aftertaste is a bit bitter.

548
00:36:17,759 --> 00:36:19,720
That's how  ujeon  tea is.

549
00:36:19,845 --> 00:36:21,680
It's made from young leaves,

550
00:36:21,805 --> 00:36:23,265
so the scent is light,

551
00:36:23,390 --> 00:36:25,142
but it leaves a slight bitterness.

552
00:36:25,267 --> 00:36:26,894
That's the charm of  ujeon  tea.

553
00:36:27,686 --> 00:36:29,062
No.

554
00:36:29,187 --> 00:36:31,356
It's because you mixed in
cheap powdered  sejak  tea.

555
00:36:35,694 --> 00:36:38,530
You were probably offered investments
with guaranteed principal.

556
00:36:39,615 --> 00:36:41,241
She promised upfront profits

557
00:36:41,366 --> 00:36:44,244
and guaranteed dividends
so you wouldn't lose money.

558
00:36:46,038 --> 00:36:47,164
But you know what?

559
00:36:47,289 --> 00:36:48,248
It's a scam.

560
00:36:48,999 --> 00:36:49,875
-What?
-What?

561
00:36:51,460 --> 00:36:52,586
Despite her appearance,

562
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:54,796
she has five fraud convictions.

563
00:36:54,922 --> 00:36:57,132
-Oh my.
-No way.

564
00:36:59,134 --> 00:37:01,386
We all have other plans, right?

565
00:37:01,511 --> 00:37:03,305
-Yes, we do.
-Oh my goodness.

566
00:37:09,895 --> 00:37:11,396
I'll call you later.

567
00:37:18,612 --> 00:37:20,572
You're still looking beautiful, Mom.

568
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:24,242
How have you been?

569
00:37:37,589 --> 00:37:38,757
What brings you here?

570
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:43,011
You acted like you'd kill me
if I ever called you.

571
00:37:43,136 --> 00:37:45,806
You know why. It's about Mi-do.

572
00:37:47,391 --> 00:37:48,809
I didn't ask her for it.

573
00:37:49,685 --> 00:37:51,728
She pitied me and helped me out.

574
00:37:55,482 --> 00:37:56,984
That's ridiculous.

575
00:37:57,109 --> 00:37:59,111
Like Mi-do would ever do that.

576
00:37:59,236 --> 00:38:00,779
So what?

577
00:38:00,904 --> 00:38:04,116
You've come to confront me
over some cash from your girl?

578
00:38:05,575 --> 00:38:06,827
Confront?

579
00:38:08,996 --> 00:38:10,622
That's a cute way to put it.

580
00:38:19,089 --> 00:38:22,759
Singapore DBJ Private Banking,
Catherine Tak.

581
00:38:25,387 --> 00:38:26,304
That's you, right?

582
00:38:32,644 --> 00:38:36,273
Since you have no assets in your name,
it took me a while to find out.

583
00:38:37,816 --> 00:38:39,776
I submitted proof to the court

584
00:38:39,901 --> 00:38:42,571
that you used Catherine Tak
as your alias for the account.

585
00:38:43,739 --> 00:38:45,240
By now,

586
00:38:45,365 --> 00:38:46,992
it's probably been frozen.

587
00:38:49,286 --> 00:38:51,079
I also got the deposit for this place

588
00:38:51,621 --> 00:38:54,916
and the one for the leased land in Hadong
provisionally attached,

589
00:38:55,042 --> 00:38:56,001
so just know that.

590
00:38:59,755 --> 00:39:00,589
Son.

591
00:39:02,049 --> 00:39:06,386
Korean law doesn't recognize debt
between parents and children.

592
00:39:06,511 --> 00:39:07,971
We're bound by blood.

593
00:39:08,096 --> 00:39:10,307
The law can't do anything about it.

594
00:39:11,141 --> 00:39:12,601
Don't you know that by now?

595
00:39:12,726 --> 00:39:14,061
Of course I know.

596
00:39:16,730 --> 00:39:17,939
That damn law.

597
00:39:19,066 --> 00:39:20,901
That damn blood tie.

598
00:39:22,652 --> 00:39:23,487
So…

599
00:39:25,530 --> 00:39:27,908
I'll use that blood tie to play God.

600
00:39:31,495 --> 00:39:32,913
Emotional instability,

601
00:39:33,830 --> 00:39:35,373
impaired judgment,

602
00:39:37,209 --> 00:39:40,337
delusional disorder,
and nervous breakdown.

603
00:39:43,048 --> 00:39:43,924
How's that?

604
00:39:45,425 --> 00:39:47,969
They're reasons to have you committed.
Do you like them?

605
00:39:49,638 --> 00:39:52,182
Because I'm your only legal guardian.

606
00:39:52,766 --> 00:39:54,142
Which means,

607
00:39:54,267 --> 00:39:57,979
I can lock you up in a psych ward
whenever I want.

608
00:39:59,481 --> 00:40:00,857
Are you crazy?

609
00:40:00,982 --> 00:40:02,526
Have you lost your mind?

610
00:40:03,151 --> 00:40:04,194
Mom.

611
00:40:05,487 --> 00:40:07,906
You shouldn't have messed with Mi-do.

612
00:40:11,493 --> 00:40:13,954
You shouldn't have messed with Mi-do.

613
00:40:27,175 --> 00:40:28,802
Detectives will be here soon.

614
00:40:31,138 --> 00:40:33,306
I have one last favor to ask.

615
00:40:35,767 --> 00:40:37,435
Don't make this any uglier.

616
00:40:40,063 --> 00:40:41,565
You can at least do that.

617
00:41:06,131 --> 00:41:07,757
Who are you to ruin this?

618
00:41:08,884 --> 00:41:10,719
I've planned this for years!

619
00:41:10,844 --> 00:41:12,804
Who do you think you are?

620
00:41:15,557 --> 00:41:17,350
You're marrying Mi-do soon, right?

621
00:41:17,934 --> 00:41:19,269
Does she know?

622
00:41:19,394 --> 00:41:21,188
About my private loans?

623
00:41:21,313 --> 00:41:22,439
It's probably…

624
00:41:24,191 --> 00:41:25,400
over 300 million won.

625
00:41:27,861 --> 00:41:29,196
You know how it is.

626
00:41:29,321 --> 00:41:31,781
They don't care about
renouncing inheritance or the law.

627
00:41:31,907 --> 00:41:33,909
They'll tear you apart to get paid.

628
00:41:34,034 --> 00:41:36,661
Still, rather than paying it back
by yourself,

629
00:41:36,786 --> 00:41:39,080
it'd be better
to pay it back together with Mi-do.

630
00:41:39,206 --> 00:41:40,332
Shut your mouth!

631
00:41:40,457 --> 00:41:42,125
Is Mi-do still filming?

632
00:41:42,709 --> 00:41:43,960
When does it come out?

633
00:41:44,085 --> 00:41:46,338
I'll do an interview from prison.

634
00:41:46,463 --> 00:41:47,714
Or maybe not?

635
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:51,551
If Mi-do makes it big,

636
00:41:51,676 --> 00:41:53,178
would that be better for me?

637
00:41:53,303 --> 00:41:55,305
I'll have to think about it.

638
00:41:57,182 --> 00:41:58,975
You think I'll go down alone?

639
00:42:00,227 --> 00:42:02,145
-I'll drag Mi-do into it.
-Stop it.

640
00:42:02,270 --> 00:42:03,980
She sent me money for two years.

641
00:42:04,105 --> 00:42:08,276
I'll go to the police
and tell them she's an accomplice.

642
00:42:08,818 --> 00:42:10,695
I'm never going down alone.

643
00:42:15,742 --> 00:42:16,660
Hey!

644
00:42:20,580 --> 00:42:22,332
Let go of my mom!

645
00:42:24,751 --> 00:42:28,421
YEONMUHEON

646
00:42:28,546 --> 00:42:29,798
Let go of my mom right now!

647
00:42:29,923 --> 00:42:31,341
Let go!

648
00:42:48,942 --> 00:42:49,901
Get up.

649
00:42:50,026 --> 00:42:53,571
-Where's the money?
-I don't have it!

650
00:42:53,697 --> 00:42:55,448
-Give it!
-I don't have it!

651
00:42:56,116 --> 00:42:57,742
-Who the hell are you?
-My son.

652
00:42:58,910 --> 00:42:59,869
You crazy bastard!

653
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:15,302
Damn it.

654
00:43:15,427 --> 00:43:17,887
Get out of my way, you fucker!

655
00:43:18,013 --> 00:43:20,223
Come here! Come here!

656
00:43:21,141 --> 00:43:22,392
Damn it!

657
00:43:22,517 --> 00:43:23,351
Ugh, seriously.

658
00:43:23,476 --> 00:43:25,270
You crazy bastard.

659
00:43:25,395 --> 00:43:26,938
Where did this bitch go?

660
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:28,606
Ugh, fuck.

661
00:43:28,732 --> 00:43:30,608
Let go! Let me go.

662
00:43:30,734 --> 00:43:35,488
You posted used phones, took the cash,
and ghosted 12 times. Is that true?

663
00:43:40,327 --> 00:43:41,661
It's all my fault.

664
00:43:43,455 --> 00:43:45,081
He studies art.

665
00:43:45,707 --> 00:43:47,542
But I don't have the means,

666
00:43:48,168 --> 00:43:50,378
so I couldn't even send him to classes.

667
00:43:52,464 --> 00:43:55,216
But since he's a minor,
he'll be released soon, right?

668
00:44:01,473 --> 00:44:02,307
Oh, dear.

669
00:44:07,103 --> 00:44:10,523
Thought you hooked a rich guy
and were paying the interest.

670
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:12,067
What's all this?

671
00:44:13,360 --> 00:44:15,528
My husband's life insurance payout
is coming.

672
00:44:15,653 --> 00:44:16,905
I'll pay you then.

673
00:44:17,030 --> 00:44:20,200
That's barely anything, isn't it?

674
00:44:21,284 --> 00:44:23,036
How will you pay me back?

675
00:44:23,161 --> 00:44:24,704
-Huh?
-Let go of my mom!

676
00:45:01,574 --> 00:45:04,452
Meet me at the 24-Hour
Mediterranean Sauna by 4:00.

677
00:45:05,412 --> 00:45:07,622
A large top and size 32 bottoms.

678
00:45:08,581 --> 00:45:11,543
A casual look
that's simple but still dapper.

679
00:45:13,086 --> 00:45:16,047
Keep the top, bottom, and jacket
under 100,000 won.

680
00:45:26,307 --> 00:45:27,934
It came out to 114,000 won.

681
00:45:28,852 --> 00:45:31,688
It's hard to get a full outfit
for 100,000 won these days.

682
00:45:33,648 --> 00:45:36,067
I hate collars like this.
They're uncomfortable.

683
00:45:39,904 --> 00:45:41,698
You knew?

684
00:45:41,823 --> 00:45:43,116
Not from the start.

685
00:45:44,325 --> 00:45:45,743
I caught a glimpse earlier.

686
00:45:46,995 --> 00:45:48,746
You were behind the inflatable tube man.

687
00:45:52,834 --> 00:45:54,794
I didn't do it on purpose.

688
00:45:54,919 --> 00:45:57,172
You suddenly took the day off.

689
00:45:58,089 --> 00:46:00,717
And you suddenly went
to the Cheonan factory last time.

690
00:46:03,803 --> 00:46:06,222
Of course, you made your intentions clear.

691
00:46:06,347 --> 00:46:09,601
But I was worried you'd get all righteous
and do something on your own.

692
00:46:09,726 --> 00:46:11,269
That would be dangerous, so…

693
00:46:11,394 --> 00:46:13,021
So you followed me from home?

694
00:46:14,814 --> 00:46:16,024
I'm sorry.

695
00:46:19,652 --> 00:46:21,654
Whatever. Keep the change.

696
00:46:24,199 --> 00:46:25,617
Let me buy you a meal.

697
00:46:28,161 --> 00:46:30,246
The pork cutlet here is really good.

698
00:46:31,122 --> 00:46:34,167
I went to middle and high school here,
so I know.

699
00:46:34,292 --> 00:46:36,002
It's really good. I'll pay.

700
00:46:38,630 --> 00:46:39,464
Deok-sun.

701
00:46:41,007 --> 00:46:43,676
Do I look like I'm in the mood
for pork cutlets?

702
00:46:44,511 --> 00:46:45,929
You saw everything earlier.

703
00:46:48,973 --> 00:46:50,391
Maybe some  sikhye  instead.

704
00:46:50,975 --> 00:46:52,810
Buy me  sikhye.  I'm craving it.

705
00:46:59,275 --> 00:47:02,695
HOT CHOCOLATE CHIPS

706
00:47:04,572 --> 00:47:05,740
-Sikhye.
-And some eggs?

707
00:47:05,865 --> 00:47:06,699
I'll have ramen.

708
00:47:08,243 --> 00:47:09,327
Park Su-a?

709
00:47:10,954 --> 00:47:13,122
It's been a while. How have you been?

710
00:47:13,248 --> 00:47:15,041
Oh, it's been a while.

711
00:47:15,166 --> 00:47:17,335
Hey, let's keep in touch.

712
00:47:17,460 --> 00:47:19,295
I heard you're at Hunmin.

713
00:47:19,420 --> 00:47:21,589
-I'm at Mugang Planning.
-I'm at Jaeu Insurance.

714
00:47:21,714 --> 00:47:24,050
We work close by.
How have we never seen each other?

715
00:47:24,175 --> 00:47:25,051
I know, right?

716
00:47:25,802 --> 00:47:27,178
When you have time,

717
00:47:28,137 --> 00:47:29,764
let's grab lunch.

718
00:47:31,349 --> 00:47:32,642
-Oh…
-Park Su-a.

719
00:47:36,771 --> 00:47:37,814
I'm her cousin.

720
00:47:38,690 --> 00:47:41,109
-Oh, hello.
-Hello.

721
00:47:41,818 --> 00:47:43,194
You coming?

722
00:47:43,319 --> 00:47:45,113
Oh, right. Coming.

723
00:47:45,238 --> 00:47:46,072
I should go.

724
00:47:46,197 --> 00:47:47,115
-Okay.
-Bye.

725
00:47:50,910 --> 00:47:52,120
That was them, right?

726
00:47:53,329 --> 00:47:56,040
The ones who stole your gym clothes
and kept your textbooks.

727
00:47:58,084 --> 00:47:59,085
How did you know?

728
00:47:59,627 --> 00:48:00,628
Your face gave it away.

729
00:48:01,713 --> 00:48:04,007
Why even respond to them?
Just ignore them.

730
00:48:08,553 --> 00:48:11,055
But usually, in a situation like this,

731
00:48:11,180 --> 00:48:13,266
wouldn't you speak up for me?

732
00:48:13,975 --> 00:48:15,935
Stop reading comic books.

733
00:48:16,060 --> 00:48:19,314
Me fighting young girls
would just be weird and pathetic.

734
00:48:19,897 --> 00:48:21,107
Yeah, yeah.

735
00:48:24,485 --> 00:48:25,862
Next time that happens,

736
00:48:25,987 --> 00:48:27,697
just repeat these three phrases.

737
00:48:28,865 --> 00:48:29,741
"Why would I?"

738
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:31,576
"So what?"

739
00:48:32,243 --> 00:48:33,161
"Who cares?"

740
00:48:33,786 --> 00:48:34,829
Got it?

741
00:48:39,083 --> 00:48:40,001
Forget it.

742
00:48:40,126 --> 00:48:41,794
I won't see them again anyway.

743
00:48:42,670 --> 00:48:44,422
Besides, it's all in the past.

744
00:48:48,551 --> 00:48:49,844
Back in high school,

745
00:48:49,969 --> 00:48:52,764
I couldn't go to the cafeteria
for three years.

746
00:48:52,889 --> 00:48:54,390
What did they say again?

747
00:48:54,515 --> 00:48:56,643
They said I might have AIDS or something.

748
00:48:57,226 --> 00:48:58,686
They made such a huge fuss.

749
00:48:58,811 --> 00:49:00,688
So I couldn't eat a proper meal

750
00:49:00,813 --> 00:49:02,440
and lived on bread and snacks.

751
00:49:02,565 --> 00:49:04,275
That's how I got by.

752
00:49:07,654 --> 00:49:09,781
That's when I started liking snacks.

753
00:49:10,448 --> 00:49:12,200
And that's also why I joined Hunmin.

754
00:49:12,992 --> 00:49:14,786
-Why tell me this now?
-What?

755
00:49:16,913 --> 00:49:17,955
Where are you going?

756
00:49:21,167 --> 00:49:22,752
Oh, I'm sorry!

757
00:49:22,877 --> 00:49:24,379
-Are you okay?
-Yes, are you?

758
00:49:24,504 --> 00:49:25,380
Darn it.

759
00:49:26,089 --> 00:49:27,465
I'm so sorry.

760
00:49:28,883 --> 00:49:31,511
Park Su-a still gives zero reaction.

761
00:49:31,636 --> 00:49:33,054
It's no fun teasing her.

762
00:49:33,179 --> 00:49:34,013
I know, right?

763
00:49:34,138 --> 00:49:35,473
Ji Su-yeon was fun.

764
00:49:35,598 --> 00:49:37,767
Yeah, Ji Su-yeon was hilarious. The…

765
00:49:50,780 --> 00:49:52,115
Mugang Planning.

766
00:49:52,240 --> 00:49:53,282
Jaeu Insurance.

767
00:49:54,575 --> 00:49:56,119
-And you?
-Oh, me?

768
00:49:56,244 --> 00:49:57,662
BQ Construction.

769
00:49:57,787 --> 00:49:59,247
BQ.

770
00:49:59,372 --> 00:50:01,207
Close to Hunmin Confectionery.

771
00:50:01,332 --> 00:50:03,418
Yes, but why…

772
00:50:05,503 --> 00:50:06,587
From now on,

773
00:50:06,713 --> 00:50:10,091
if you ever come across Park Su-a,
don't you dare talk to her. Just walk by.

774
00:50:12,635 --> 00:50:15,304
Don't pretend to be friendly
just to insult her.

775
00:50:17,098 --> 00:50:18,641
What do you mean?

776
00:50:18,766 --> 00:50:20,893
You can't do this, even as her cousin.

777
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:24,605
Did Park Su-a say that we bullied her?

778
00:50:25,314 --> 00:50:27,400
We never did anything like that.

779
00:50:27,525 --> 00:50:28,776
You never did?

780
00:50:29,986 --> 00:50:30,862
Hey.

781
00:50:31,446 --> 00:50:33,030
I asked if you never did.

782
00:50:34,490 --> 00:50:35,825
I'm warning you.

783
00:50:36,617 --> 00:50:40,371
If you ever run into Park Su-a
on the street and speak to her,

784
00:50:41,789 --> 00:50:42,999
all three of you

785
00:50:44,083 --> 00:50:45,626
will seriously pay for it.

786
00:50:48,463 --> 00:50:49,464
Mr. Namgung…

787
00:50:50,798 --> 00:50:51,632
Ho!

788
00:50:55,178 --> 00:50:56,512
Stop it. Let's go.

789
00:50:56,637 --> 00:50:58,055
You've been warned.

790
00:50:58,181 --> 00:50:59,474
Don't talk to her.

791
00:51:01,684 --> 00:51:04,187
Wow, this is unbelievable.

792
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:07,315
Hey, Park Su-a,
you should apologize to us.

793
00:51:10,234 --> 00:51:11,402
Why would I?

794
00:51:13,029 --> 00:51:15,531
Did you not hear
what your cousin just said?

795
00:51:15,656 --> 00:51:17,283
He completely insulted us.

796
00:51:17,408 --> 00:51:18,242
So what?

797
00:51:18,367 --> 00:51:20,912
He really spooked us.
Do you have any idea?

798
00:51:21,037 --> 00:51:22,371
Who cares?

799
00:51:31,172 --> 00:51:32,507
Let's go.

800
00:51:40,389 --> 00:51:42,183
Yeah, I'm chopping them now.

801
00:51:42,975 --> 00:51:45,144
So I put them in all at once?

802
00:51:45,686 --> 00:51:48,147
The onions, carrots… And potatoes?

803
00:51:48,272 --> 00:51:49,524
Oh, okay.

804
00:51:49,649 --> 00:51:50,858
And green onions?

805
00:51:50,983 --> 00:51:51,818
Oh, and…

806
00:51:53,402 --> 00:51:54,779
I'll call you back.

807
00:51:56,572 --> 00:51:58,115
Hey, Director Lee!

808
00:51:58,241 --> 00:51:59,283
Open the door.

809
00:51:59,951 --> 00:52:01,452
Open up!

810
00:52:02,829 --> 00:52:05,790
Open the door! Open up!

811
00:52:05,915 --> 00:52:08,084
Open the door!

812
00:52:20,346 --> 00:52:22,765
Ms. Song, what are you doing?

813
00:52:22,890 --> 00:52:25,351
Why aren't you coming back?

814
00:52:26,435 --> 00:52:28,938
Are you trying to torture me to death?

815
00:52:29,063 --> 00:52:32,233
If you keep bothering me, I just might.

816
00:52:33,276 --> 00:52:34,193
I knew it.

817
00:52:35,486 --> 00:52:36,779
I figured as much.

818
00:52:37,947 --> 00:52:39,490
You're getting revenge on me.

819
00:52:44,287 --> 00:52:46,664
I was out of my mind back then.

820
00:52:46,789 --> 00:52:49,333
I'll keep your secret, Ms. Song.

821
00:52:49,458 --> 00:52:50,793
So don't worry and leave.

822
00:52:53,379 --> 00:52:54,964
Suddenly acting all nice.

823
00:52:56,257 --> 00:52:58,342
Just tell me to get on my knees.

824
00:52:58,467 --> 00:53:00,386
No, you don't need to.

825
00:53:00,511 --> 00:53:02,763
I don't want to see you anymore. Just go.

826
00:53:02,889 --> 00:53:04,307
What do you want?

827
00:53:04,432 --> 00:53:05,266
Is it money?

828
00:53:05,933 --> 00:53:08,477
Just say so. Stop pretending to be nice!

829
00:53:17,236 --> 00:53:18,404
Hey!

830
00:53:31,250 --> 00:53:35,129
If you ever come back here again,
I won't let you get away with it.

831
00:53:35,254 --> 00:53:36,881
This is your last warning.

832
00:53:48,142 --> 00:53:50,519
Ugh, Song Hae-na, seriously.

833
00:53:52,688 --> 00:53:54,440
Is she trying to test me or…

834
00:53:55,816 --> 00:53:58,778
Song Hae-na is here, right?

835
00:54:32,603 --> 00:54:34,188
Song Hae-na isn't here.

836
00:54:34,772 --> 00:54:37,483
She just left.
You can catch her if you go now.

837
00:54:37,608 --> 00:54:40,069
I only believe things
I see with my own eyes.

838
00:54:45,866 --> 00:54:46,701
By the way…

839
00:54:49,620 --> 00:54:50,830
why the sudden formal tone?

840
00:54:52,999 --> 00:54:55,376
I no longer hold the upper hand.

841
00:54:55,501 --> 00:54:57,003
Go tell Song Hae-na

842
00:54:57,628 --> 00:55:00,006
that I will never breathe a word about it.

843
00:55:01,007 --> 00:55:03,259
I'm blocking her number now,

844
00:55:03,384 --> 00:55:05,386
so tell her not to try calling.

845
00:55:06,512 --> 00:55:08,264
Did you block my number too?

846
00:55:13,102 --> 00:55:14,186
No wonder.

847
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:17,565
I couldn't get through to you.

848
00:55:18,816 --> 00:55:20,818
I thought about using another phone,

849
00:55:20,943 --> 00:55:22,945
but my pride wouldn't let me.

850
00:55:25,031 --> 00:55:26,073
Still…

851
00:55:32,413 --> 00:55:33,706
I lost again.

852
00:55:38,753 --> 00:55:41,422
Do you think I came here
to catch Song Hae-na?

853
00:55:42,506 --> 00:55:43,799
I'm not an idiot.

854
00:56:05,404 --> 00:56:06,405
It was so annoying.

855
00:56:08,616 --> 00:56:10,201
I kept thinking about it.

856
00:56:15,456 --> 00:56:17,166
So I came to check.

857
00:56:19,126 --> 00:56:21,295
If I just lost my mind that night,

858
00:56:22,004 --> 00:56:24,298
or if I'm still out of my mind.

859
00:56:30,471 --> 00:56:33,891
Besides the deleted scenes
you want to hide from others,

860
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:36,560
there are other hidden scenes.

861
00:56:37,311 --> 00:56:39,522
The ones that even I want to forget.

862
00:56:39,647 --> 00:56:41,690
The ones I want to tear to pieces.

863
00:56:42,858 --> 00:56:44,777
The ones I want to keep hidden.

864
00:56:44,902 --> 00:56:46,570
The ones they must never know about.

865
00:56:46,695 --> 00:56:48,030
Those kinds of untold stories.

866
00:57:19,145 --> 00:57:22,773
I can't help but think
you're hiding something.

867
00:57:25,484 --> 00:57:28,487
What is it that makes you refuse
to return as a director

868
00:57:30,447 --> 00:57:32,074
and put me through such hell?

869
00:57:38,205 --> 00:57:39,790
You don't want to direct, do you?

870
00:57:41,667 --> 00:57:43,335
You're scared, aren't you?

871
00:57:53,137 --> 00:57:54,889
I knew it. You're scared.

872
00:57:57,600 --> 00:57:58,684
No, I'm not.

873
00:58:00,352 --> 00:58:01,729
That's not it.

874
00:58:03,022 --> 00:58:04,356
Yes, you are.

875
00:58:04,940 --> 00:58:06,150
You want to run away.

876
00:58:07,109 --> 00:58:08,903
You're scared and terrified.

877
00:58:10,779 --> 00:58:12,656
But you feel bad for your boyfriend,

878
00:58:12,781 --> 00:58:14,909
so you're too ashamed to do it.

879
00:58:16,619 --> 00:58:17,536
Am I wrong?

880
00:58:18,871 --> 00:58:19,955
You're wrong.

881
00:58:27,254 --> 00:58:28,672
Want me to help you escape?

882
00:58:31,300 --> 00:58:34,637
You were desperate enough
to go beg Song Hae-na,

883
00:58:36,138 --> 00:58:38,224
but I got in the way and ruined it.

884
00:58:40,142 --> 00:58:44,230
You can say you had the talent
but just got unlucky.

885
00:58:48,817 --> 00:58:51,153
You got tangled up with some crazy guy,

886
00:58:52,321 --> 00:58:54,073
and got completely screwed over.

887
00:58:58,202 --> 00:59:00,788
Burying a rookie director
before they even start

888
00:59:00,913 --> 00:59:03,540
is incredibly easy for me.

889
00:59:09,255 --> 00:59:11,173
Why would you go that far for me?

890
00:59:14,009 --> 00:59:15,678
What do you want from me?

891
00:59:19,098 --> 00:59:20,641
One thing is for sure.

892
00:59:22,601 --> 00:59:24,103
It's not because of the settlement.

893
01:00:15,946 --> 01:00:17,072
Attorney Han.

894
01:00:38,719 --> 01:00:41,138
Did he leave? I thought he was here.

895
01:00:45,601 --> 01:00:46,727
Attorney Han.

896
01:00:47,895 --> 01:00:50,564
I'm calling about the report on Jisang.

897
01:00:50,689 --> 01:00:52,649
There's something you need to check.

898
01:00:52,775 --> 01:00:54,777
I'm home. Email it to me.

899
01:00:54,902 --> 01:00:56,403
I'll check and call you back.

900
01:02:02,136 --> 01:02:03,262
I…

901
01:02:03,929 --> 01:02:05,973
kissed this man.

902
01:03:11,830 --> 01:03:14,958
Mi-do cries
whenever she sees me these days.

903
01:03:15,083 --> 01:03:15,918
Is she going through menopause?

904
01:03:16,043 --> 01:03:16,877
EXPAT POSITION IN PARIS

905
01:03:17,002 --> 01:03:19,171
Are you getting married, Mr. Namgung?
You are, right?

906
01:03:20,422 --> 01:03:21,757
I'll let you quit directing.

907
01:03:22,299 --> 01:03:23,550
Let's have some fun for a bit.

908
01:03:23,675 --> 01:03:25,844
Did Mr. Namgung take out a private loan?

909
01:03:25,969 --> 01:03:27,971
I already died when I was seven,

910
01:03:28,096 --> 01:03:30,057
so I'm living on borrowed time.

911
01:03:30,182 --> 01:03:31,350
Mess with me and see.

912
01:03:31,475 --> 01:03:33,936
I'll show you how crazy I can get.

913
01:03:34,645 --> 01:03:36,605
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
